      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__packet_1ac8d42bcd4a44e078047ccd7291059238" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>unsigned int</type>
        <definition>unsigned int length</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>length</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_packet::length</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Length of <ref refid="structndigo__packet_1a8973e4107f0b644d540e9c0725574c3d" kindref="member">ndigo_packet::data</ref> in units of 64 bit. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Number of 64-bit elements (each containing 4 samples) in the data array as long as <ref refid="structndigo__packet_1aa5044999f3339d2ba3b1bf22fa6cfe95" kindref="member">ndigo_packet::type</ref> &lt; <ref refid="group__usedtypedefs_1gaef7566e384760955b43719deb3d906e7" kindref="member">NDIGO_PACKET_TYPE_TIMESTAMP_ONLY</ref>.</para>
<para>If <ref refid="structndigo__packet_1aa5044999f3339d2ba3b1bf22fa6cfe95" kindref="member">ndigo_packet::type</ref> = <ref refid="group__usedtypedefs_1gaef7566e384760955b43719deb3d906e7" kindref="member">NDIGO_PACKET_TYPE_TIMESTAMP_ONLY</ref>. this is the pattern of trigger sources that where active in the clock cycle given by <ref refid="structndigo__packet_1a465bef81f6478756e5443025b1f2ddfa" kindref="member">ndigo_packet::timestamp</ref>. Bits are set according to the trigger sources, i.e. bit 0 is set if trigger <ref refid="group__sourcedefs_1gad57ed5dbf34f66af23756728e5351abe" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_SOURCE_A0</ref> was active, bit 29 is set if <ref refid="group__sourcedefs_1ga5058bd6fdb5e3eaf6ab6e54942658d56" kindref="member">NDIGO_TRIGGER_SOURCE_BUS3_PE</ref> was active, etc, as listed in <ref refid="structndigo__trigger__block_1a09bf0a0c15c4905391944154b116a637" kindref="member">ndigo_trigger_block::sources</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_common_interface.h" line="425" column="18" bodyfile="ndigo_common_interface.h" bodystart="425" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__packet_1a465bef81f6478756e5443025b1f2ddfa" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>uint64_t</type>
        <definition>uint64_t timestamp</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>timestamp</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_packet::timestamp</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Timestamp in ps. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>ADC channels A to D: timestamp of the last word in the packet.</para>
<para>TDC channel (<ref refid="structndigo__packet_1adc18ec7f4fcbc00d327f412b44a6385d" kindref="member">ndigo_packet::channel</ref> = 4): timestamp of the trigger event (falling edge) of the TDC channel. When <ref refid="ndigo__common__interface_8h_1aac09ea1a0bea1fb23cc5e25b7af9cd36" kindref="member">ndigo_process_tdc_packet()</ref> is called once on the the packet, the timestamp is replaced with the precise timestamp for the edge.</para>
<para>Timestamp channel (<ref refid="structndigo__packet_1adc18ec7f4fcbc00d327f412b44a6385d" kindref="member">ndigo_packet::channel</ref> = 5): timestamp of the trigger event. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_common_interface.h" line="439" column="14" bodyfile="ndigo_common_interface.h" bodystart="439" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
